# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, because qubit 0 was in a superposition state, the circuit evaluated the "
"function for *both* $x=0$ and $x=1$ *at the same time* — something classical"
" computers cannot do! But the catch comes when we want to learn about the "
"function $f(x)$ — when we measure the qubits, we collapse their state. If "
"you select \"shots = 1\" to only run the circuit once, you will only see one"
" bar in the histogram above, and your information about the function will be"
" incomplete.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, kerana qubit 0 berada dalam keadaan superposisi, litar menilai fungsi "
"untuk *kedua-dua* $x=0$ dan $x=1$ *pada masa yang sama* — sesuatu yang tidak"
" dapat dilakukan oleh komputer klasik! Tetapi masalahnya timbul apabila kita"
" ingin mengetahui tentang fungsi $f(x)$ — apabila kita mengukur qubit, kita "
"meruntuhkan keadaannya. Jika anda memilih \"shots = 1\" untuk hanya "
"menjalankan litar sekali, anda hanya akan melihat satu bar dalam histogram "
"di atas, dan maklumat anda tentang fungsi tersebut akan tidak lengkap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How many times must we run the above algorithm to learn the function $f(x)$?"
" Is this any better than the classical case? Would you rather have a "
"classical or quantum computer to solve this problem?\n"
msgstr ""
"Berapa kali kita perlu menjalankan algoritma di atas untuk mengetahui fungsi"
" $f(x)$? Adakah ini lebih baik daripada kes klasik? Adakah anda lebih suka "
"mempunyai komputer klasik atau kuantum untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the measurement will collapse the superposition and return only one "
"value, we need to run the circuit *at least* twice to return both outputs of"
" the function $f(0)$ and $f(1)$. Best case, this performs as well as the "
"classical case, where we compute both $f(0)$ and $f(1)$ in the first two "
"queries. But there's a chance that we'll need to run it more than two times,"
" since the final measurement is probabilistic and might return the same "
"$f(x)$ value the first two times. I would rather have a classical computer "
"in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan pengukuran akan meruntuhkan superposisi dan hanya mengembalikan"
" satu nilai, kita perlu menjalankan litar *sekurang-kurangnya* dua kali "
"untuk mendapatkan kedua-dua output fungsi $f(0)$ dan $f(1)$. Dalam kes "
"terbaik, ini berjalan sama baiknya dengan kes klasik, di mana kita mengira "
"kedua-dua $f(0)$ dan $f(1)$ dalam dua pertanyaan pertama. Tetapi ada "
"kemungkinan kita perlu menjalankannya lebih daripada dua kali, kerana "
"pengukuran akhir adalah kebarangkalian dan mungkin mengembalikan nilai "
"$f(x)$ yang sama dua kali pertama. Saya lebih suka mempunyai komputer klasik"
" dalam kes ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, while quantum parallelism can be powerful when used in the right way, it"
" is not correct to say that a quantum computer works just like a massive, "
"classical parallel processor. The act of measurement collapses the quantum "
"states, so we can only ever access a single output of the computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, walaupun keselarian kuantum boleh menjadi berkuasa apabila digunakan "
"dengan cara yang betul, tidak tepat untuk mengatakan bahawa komputer kuantum"
" berfungsi seperti pemproses selari klasik yang besar. Tindakan pengukuran "
"meruntuhkan keadaan kuantum, jadi kita hanya boleh mengakses satu output "
"pengiraan pada bila-bila masa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch's algorithm {#deutschs-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma Deutsch {#deutschs-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While quantum parallelism alone doesn't give us an advantage over classical "
"computers, we can pair this with another quantum phenomena, interference, to"
" achieve a speed-up. The algorithm now known as \"Deutsch's algorithm\" is "
"the first example of an algorithm that accomplishes this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun keselarian kuantum sahaja tidak memberi kita kelebihan berbanding "
"komputer klasik, kita boleh menggabungkannya dengan fenomena kuantum lain, "
"iaitu interferens, untuk mencapai percepatan. Algoritma yang kini dikenali "
"sebagai \"algoritma Deutsch\" adalah contoh pertama algoritma yang mencapai "
"perkara ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The problem {#the-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah {#the-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here was the problem:\n"
msgstr "Inilah masalahnya:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given an input bit, $x = \\{0,1\\}$, and an input function $f(x) = "
"\\{0,1\\}$, determine whether the function is *balanced* or *constant*. That"
" is, if it's balanced, then the output of the function is 0 half the time "
"and 1 the other half the time. If it's constant, then the output of the "
"function is either always 0 or always 1. Recall the table of four possible "
"functions taking a single bit to another a single bit:\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan satu bit input, $x = \\{0,1\\}$, dan fungsi input $f(x) = "
"\\{0,1\\}$, tentukan sama ada fungsi tersebut adalah *seimbang* atau "
"*malar*. Iaitu, jika ia seimbang, maka output fungsi adalah 0 separuh masa "
"dan 1 separuh masa yang lain. Jika ia malar, maka output fungsi adalah "
"sentiasa 0 atau sentiasa 1. Ingat semula jadual empat fungsi yang mungkin "
"mengambil satu bit kepada satu bit lain:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first and the last functions, $f_1(x)$ and $f_4(x)$, are constant, while"
" the middle two functions, $f_2(x)$ and $f_3(x)$, are balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi pertama dan terakhir, $f_1(x)$ dan $f_4(x)$, adalah malar, manakala "
"dua fungsi di tengah, $f_2(x)$ dan $f_3(x)$, adalah seimbang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The algorithm {#the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma tersebut {#the-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way Deutsch approached this problem was through the \"query model.\" In "
"the query model, the input function ($f_i(x)$ above) is contained in a "
"\"black box\" — we don't have direct access to its contents, but we can "
"query the black box and it will give us the output of the function. We "
"sometimes say that an \"oracle\" provides this information. See [Lesson 1: "
"Quantum Query Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/introduction) of the Fundamentals of "
"Quantum Algorithms course for more on the query model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara Deutsch mendekati masalah ini adalah melalui \"model pertanyaan.\" "
"Dalam model pertanyaan, fungsi input ($f_i(x)$ di atas) terkandung dalam "
"sebuah \"kotak hitam\" — kita tidak mempunyai akses langsung kepada "
"kandungannya, tetapi kita boleh membuat pertanyaan kepada kotak hitam "
"tersebut dan ia akan memberikan output fungsi tersebut kepada kita. Kita "
"kadangkala berkata bahawa sebuah \"oracle\" menyediakan maklumat ini. Lihat "
"[Pelajaran 1: Algoritma Pertanyaan Kuantum](/learning/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/introduction) dalam kursus "
"Asas Algoritma Kuantum untuk maklumat lanjut tentang model pertanyaan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To determine whether a quantum algorithm is more efficient than a classical "
"algorithm in the query model, we can simply compare the number of queries we"
" need to make of the black box in each case. In the classical case, in order"
" to know if the function contained in the black box were balanced or "
"constant, we would need to query the box two times to get both $f(0)$ and "
"$f(1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menentukan sama ada algoritma kuantum lebih cekap daripada algoritma "
"klasik dalam model pertanyaan, kita boleh membandingkan bilangan pertanyaan "
"yang perlu kita buat kepada kotak hitam dalam setiap kes. Dalam kes klasik, "
"untuk mengetahui sama ada fungsi yang terkandung dalam kotak hitam adalah "
"seimbang atau malar, kita perlu membuat pertanyaan kepada kotak tersebut dua"
" kali untuk mendapatkan kedua-dua $f(0)$ dan $f(1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Deutsch's quantum algorithm, though, he found a way to get the "
"information with only one query! He made one adjustment to the \"quantum "
"parallelism\" circuit above, so that he prepared a superposition state on "
"*both* qubits, instead of only on qubit 0. Then the two outputs of the "
"function, $f(0)$ and $f(1)$ interfered to return 0 if they were either both "
"0 or both 1 (the function was constant), and returned 1 if they were "
"different (the function was balanced). In this way, Deutsch could "
"differentiate between a constant and a balanced function with a single "
"query.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam algoritma kuantum Deutsch, beliau menemui cara untuk mendapatkan "
"maklumat dengan hanya satu pertanyaan! Beliau membuat satu penyelarasan pada"
" litar \"keselarian kuantum\" di atas, supaya beliau menyediakan keadaan "
"superposisi pada *kedua-dua* qubit, bukan hanya pada qubit 0 sahaja. "
"Kemudian dua output fungsi, $f(0)$ dan $f(1)$ berinterferensi untuk "
"mengembalikan 0 jika keduanya 0 atau keduanya 1 (fungsi adalah malar), dan "
"mengembalikan 1 jika keduanya berbeza (fungsi adalah seimbang). Dengan cara "
"ini, Deutsch boleh membezakan antara fungsi malar dan seimbang dengan satu "
"pertanyaan sahaja.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a circuit diagram of Deutsch's algorithm:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah gambar rajah litar algoritma Deutsch:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit diagram of Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/Deutsch_algo.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![litar diagram of Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/Deutsch_algo.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To understand how this algorithm works, let's look at the quantum states of "
"the qubits at the three points noted on the diagram above. Try to work out "
"the states for yourself before clicking to view the answers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memahami bagaimana algoritma ini berfungsi, mari kita lihat keadaan "
"kuantum qubit pada tiga titik yang dicatat pada gambar rajah di atas. Cuba "
"usahakan keadaan-keadaan itu sendiri sebelum mengklik untuk melihat "
"jawapannya:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is the state $|\\pi_1\\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "Apakah keadaan $|\\pi_1\\rangle$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying a Hadamard transforms the state $|0\\rangle$ to "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ and the state $|1\\rangle$ to"
"  $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$. So, the full state becomes:"
" $|\\pi_1\\rangle = "
"[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]$\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan Hadamard mengubah keadaan $|0\\rangle$ kepada "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ dan keadaan $|1\\rangle$ "
"kepada $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$. Jadi, keadaan penuh "
"menjadi: $|\\pi_1\\rangle = "
"[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is the state $|\\pi_2\\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "Apakah keadaan $|\\pi_2\\rangle$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we apply $U_f$, remember what it does. It will change the state of qubit 1 based on the state of qubit 0. So, it makes sense to factor the state of qubit 0 out: $|\\pi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)|0\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)|1\\rangle$. Then, if $f(0)=f(1)$, the two terms will transform in the same way and the relative sign between the two terms remains positive, but if $f(0)\\neq f(1)$, then that means the second term will pick up a minus sign relative to the first term, changing the state of qubit 0 from $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ to $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$. So:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\pi_2\\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}] & \\text{if} & f(0) = f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}] &\\text{if} & f(0) \\neq f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita menggunakan $U_f$, ingat semula apa yang dilakukannya. Ia akan mengubah keadaan qubit 1 berdasarkan keadaan qubit 0. Jadi, masuk akal untuk memfaktorkan keadaan qubit 0: $|\\pi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)|0\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)|1\\rangle$. Kemudian, jika $f(0)=f(1)$, kedua-dua sebutan akan berubah dengan cara yang sama dan tanda relatif antara kedua-dua sebutan kekal positif, tetapi jika $f(0)\\neq f(1)$, maka ini bermakna sebutan kedua akan mengambil tanda negatif relatif terhadap sebutan pertama, mengubah keadaan qubit 0 dari $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ kepada $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$. Jadi:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\pi_2\\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}] & \\text{if} & f(0) = f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}][\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}] &\\text{if} & f(0) \\neq f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is the state $|\\pi_3\\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "Apakah keadaan $|\\pi_3\\rangle$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, the state of qubit 0 is either "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ or "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$, depending on the function. "
"Applying the Hadamard will yield either $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$, "
"respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, keadaan qubit 0 adalah sama ada "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ atau "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$, bergantung pada fungsi "
"tersebut. Menggunakan Hadamard akan menghasilkan sama ada $|0\\rangle$ atau "
"$|1\\rangle$, masing-masing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\pi_3\\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]|0\\rangle & \\text{if} & f(0) = f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]|1\\rangle &\\text{if} & f(0) \\neq f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\pi_3\\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]|0\\rangle & \\text{if} & f(0) = f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\pm[\\frac{|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}]|1\\rangle &\\text{if} & f(0) \\neq f(1) \\\\\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking through your answers for the above questions, note that something a "
"bit surprising happens. Although $U_f$ does nothing explicitly to the state "
"of qubit 0, because it changes qubit 1 based on the state of qubit 0, it can"
" happen that this causes a phase shift in qubit 0. This is known as the "
"\"phase-kickback\" phenomenon, and is discussed in more detail in [Lesson 1:"
" Quantum Query Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/introduction) of the Fundamentals of "
"Quantum Algorithms course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Melihat jawapan anda untuk soalan-soalan di atas, perhatikan bahawa sesuatu "
"yang agak mengejutkan berlaku. Walaupun $U_f$ tidak melakukan apa-apa secara"
" eksplisit pada keadaan qubit 0, kerana ia mengubah qubit 1 berdasarkan "
"keadaan qubit 0, boleh berlaku bahawa ini menyebabkan peralihan fasa pada "
"qubit 0. Ini dikenali sebagai fenomena \"phase-kickback\", dan dibincangkan "
"dengan lebih terperinci dalam [Pelajaran 1: Algoritma Pertanyaan "
"Kuantum](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-"
"algorithms/introduction) dalam kursus Asas Algoritma Kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we understand how this algorithm works, let's implement it with "
"Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah memahami cara algoritma ini berfungsi, mari kita laksanakannya "
"dengan Qiskit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/4d9129df-f2ef-4f94-9508-21ed986fd823-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/4d9129df-f2ef-4f94-9508-21ed986fd823-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm {#the-deutsch-jozsa-algorithm-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm was an important first step in demonstrating how a "
"quantum computer might be more efficient than a classical computer, but it "
"was only a modest improvement: it required just one query, compared to two "
"in the classical case. In 1992, Deutsch and his colleague, Richard Jozsa, "
"extended the original two-qubit algorithm to more qubits. The problem "
"remained the same: determine whether a function is *balanced* or *constant*."
" But this time, the function goes from $n$ bits to a single bit. Either the "
"function returns 0 and 1 an equal number of times (it's *balanced*) or the "
"function returns always 1 or always 0 (it's *constant*).\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch merupakan langkah pertama yang penting dalam menunjukkan "
"bagaimana komputer kuantum boleh lebih cekap daripada komputer klasik, "
"tetapi ia hanyalah satu peningkatan yang sederhana: ia hanya memerlukan satu"
" pertanyaan, berbanding dua dalam kes klasik. Pada tahun 1992, Deutsch dan "
"rakannya, Richard Jozsa, mengembangkan algoritma dua-qubit asal kepada lebih"
" banyak qubit. Masalahnya tetap sama: tentukan sama ada fungsi adalah "
"*seimbang* atau *malar*. Tetapi kali ini, fungsi tersebut bergerak dari $n$ "
"bit kepada satu bit. Sama ada fungsi mengembalikan 0 dan 1 dalam bilangan "
"yang sama (ia *seimbang*) atau fungsi sentiasa mengembalikan 1 atau sentiasa"
" 0 (ia *malar*).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a circuit diagram of the algorithm:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah gambar rajah litar untuk algoritma ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![DJ_algo.png](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/deutsch-"
"jozsa/DJ_algo.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![DJ_algo.png](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/deutsch-"
"jozsa/DJ_algo.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This algorithm works in the same way as Deutsch's algorithm: the phase-"
"kickback allows one to read out the state of qubit 0 to determine whether "
"the function is constant or balanced. It's a bit trickier to see than for "
"the two-qubit Deutsch's algorithm case, since the states will include sums "
"over the $n$ qubits, and so working out those states will be left as an "
"optional exercise for you at the end of the module. The algorithm will "
"return a bitstring of all 0's if the function is constant, and a bitstring "
"containing at least one 1 if the function is balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma ini berfungsi dengan cara yang sama seperti algoritma Deutsch: "
"phase-kickback membolehkan seseorang membaca keadaan qubit 0 untuk "
"menentukan sama ada fungsi itu malar atau seimbang. Ini sedikit lebih rumit "
"untuk dilihat berbanding kes algoritma Deutsch dua-qubit, kerana keadaan "
"akan merangkumi jumlah ke atas $n$ qubit, jadi mengira keadaan tersebut akan"
" ditinggalkan sebagai latihan pilihan untuk anda di hujung modul. Algoritma "
"akan mengembalikan bitstring yang semuanya 0 jika fungsi adalah malar, dan "
"bitstring yang mengandungi sekurang-kurangnya satu 1 jika fungsi adalah "
"seimbang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see how the algorithm works in Qiskit, first, we need to generate our "
"oracle: the random function that is guaranteed to be either constant or "
"balanced. The code below will generate a balanced function 50% of the time, "
"and a constant function 50% of the time. Don't worry if you don't entirely "
"follow the code — it's complicated and not necessary for our understanding "
"of the quantum algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melihat cara algoritma berfungsi dalam Qiskit, mula-mula, kita perlu "
"menjana oracle kita: fungsi rawak yang dijamin sama ada malar atau seimbang."
" Kod di bawah akan menjana fungsi seimbang 50% daripada masa, dan fungsi "
"malar 50% daripada masa. Jangan risau jika anda tidak sepenuhnya memahami "
"kod ini — ia rumit dan tidak perlu untuk pemahaman kita tentang algoritma "
"kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/ca2a51c0-3e62-4536-b891-0834e325a3d6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/ca2a51c0-3e62-4536-b891-0834e325a3d6-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the oracle function, which is either balanced or constant. Can you "
"see by looking at it whether the output on the last qubit depends on the "
"values put in for the first $n$ qubits? If the output for the last qubit "
"depends on the first $n$ qubits, can you tell if that dependent output is "
"balanced or not?\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah fungsi oracle, yang sama ada seimbang atau malar. Bolehkah anda "
"lihat dengan melihatnya sama ada output pada qubit terakhir bergantung pada "
"nilai yang dimasukkan untuk $n$ qubit pertama? Jika output untuk qubit "
"terakhir bergantung pada $n$ qubit pertama, bolehkah anda memberitahu sama "
"ada output yang bergantung itu seimbang atau tidak?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can tell whether the function is balanced or constant by looking at the "
"above circuit, but remember, for the sake of this problem, we think of this "
"function as a \"black box.\" We can't peek into the box to look at the "
"circuit diagram. Instead, we need to query the box.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh mengetahui sama ada fungsi itu seimbang atau malar dengan melihat"
" litar di atas, tetapi ingat, untuk tujuan masalah ini, kita menganggap "
"fungsi ini sebagai \"kotak hitam.\" Kita tidak boleh mengintip ke dalam "
"kotak untuk melihat gambar rajah litar. Sebaliknya, kita perlu membuat "
"pertanyaan pada kotak itu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To query the box, we use the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm and determine whether "
"the function is constant or balanced:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk membuat pertanyaan pada kotak tersebut, kita menggunakan algoritma "
"Deutsch-Jozsa dan menentukan sama ada fungsi itu malar atau seimbang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/fe7ee688-f052-4a7e-bcc7-a14bea57e5c6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/fe7ee688-f052-4a7e-bcc7-a14bea57e5c6-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/bf3aedfa-7454-424e-85cb-c446a8918417-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/deutsch-jozsa/extracted-"
"outputs/bf3aedfa-7454-424e-85cb-c446a8918417-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Above, the first line of the output is the bitstring of measurement "
"outcomes. The second line outputs whether the bitstring implies that the "
"function was balanced or constant. If the bitstring contained all zeroes, "
"then it was constant; if not, it was balanced. So, with just a single run of"
" the above quantum circuit, we can determine whether the function is "
"constant or balanced!\n"
msgstr ""
"Di atas, baris pertama output adalah bitstring hasil pengukuran. Baris kedua"
" mengeluarkan sama ada bitstring menunjukkan fungsi tersebut seimbang atau "
"malar. Jika bitstring mengandungi semua sifar, maka ia adalah malar; jika "
"tidak, ia adalah seimbang. Jadi, dengan hanya satu jalankan litar kuantum di"
" atas, kita boleh menentukan sama ada fungsi itu malar atau seimbang!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Semak pemahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How many queries would it take a classical computer to determine with 100% "
"certainty whether a function were constant or balanced? Remember, "
"classically, a single query only allows you to apply the function to a "
"single bitstring.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berapa banyak pertanyaan yang diperlukan oleh komputer klasik untuk "
"menentukan dengan kepastian 100% sama ada fungsi itu malar atau seimbang? "
"Ingat, secara klasik, satu pertanyaan hanya membolehkan anda menggunakan "
"fungsi pada satu bitstring tunggal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $2^n$ possible bitstrings to check, and in the worst case, you "
"would need to test $2^n/2+1$ of these. For example, if the function were "
"constant, and you kept measuring \"1\" as the output of the function, then "
"you couldn't be certain that it was truly constant until you checked over "
"half of the results. Before then, you might have just been very unlucky to "
"keep measuring \"1\" on a balanced function. It's like flipping a coin over "
"and over and it landing heads every time. It's unlikely, but not "
"impossible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat $2^n$ bitstring yang mungkin untuk diperiksa, dan dalam kes "
"terburuk, anda perlu menguji $2^n/2+1$ daripadanya. Sebagai contoh, jika "
"fungsi itu malar, dan anda terus mengukur \"1\" sebagai output fungsi, maka "
"anda tidak boleh pasti bahawa ia benar-benar malar sehingga anda memeriksa "
"lebih daripada separuh hasil. Sebelum itu, anda mungkin sahaja sangat malang"
" kerana terus mengukur \"1\" pada fungsi seimbang. Ia seperti melempar duit "
"syiling berulang kali dan ia jatuh pada kepala setiap kali. Ia tidak "
"mungkin, tetapi bukan mustahil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How would your above answer change if you just had to just measure until one"
" outcome (balanced or constant) is more likely than the other? How many "
"queries would it take in this case?\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana jawapan anda di atas akan berubah jika anda hanya perlu mengukur "
"sehingga satu hasil (seimbang atau malar) lebih mungkin daripada yang lain? "
"Berapa banyak pertanyaan yang diperlukan dalam kes ini?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, you could just measure twice. If the two measurements are "
"different, you know the function is balanced. If the two measurements are "
"the same, then it could be balanced, or it could be constant. The "
"probability that it's balanced with this set of measurements is: "
"$\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{2^n /2 - 1}{2^n-1}$. This is less than 1/2, so it's more"
" likely that the function is constant in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes ini, anda hanya perlu mengukur dua kali. Jika dua pengukuran "
"berbeza, anda tahu fungsi itu seimbang. Jika kedua-dua pengukuran sama, maka"
" ia mungkin seimbang, atau ia mungkin malar. Kebarangkalian bahawa ia "
"seimbang dengan set pengukuran ini adalah: $\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{2^n /2 - "
"1}{2^n-1}$. Ini kurang daripada 1/2, jadi fungsi itu lebih mungkin malar "
"dalam kes ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm demonstrated an exponential speed-up over a "
"*deterministic* classical algorithm (one that returns the answer with 100% "
"certainty), but no significant speed-up over a *probabilistic* one (one that"
" returns a result that is *likely* to be the correct answer).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa menunjukkan percepatan eksponen berbanding "
"algoritma klasik *deterministik* (yang mengembalikan jawapan dengan "
"kepastian 100%), tetapi tiada percepatan yang ketara berbanding algoritma "
"*kebarangkalian* (yang mengembalikan hasil yang *mungkin* merupakan jawapan "
"yang betul).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Bernstein - Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Bernstein - Vazirani {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In 1997, Ethan Bernstein and Umesh Vazirani used the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm"
" to solve a more specific, restricted problem compared to the Deutsch-Jozsa "
"problem. Rather than simply try to distinguish between two different classes"
" of functions, as in the D-J case, Bernstein and Vazirani used the Deutsch-"
"Jozsa algorithm to actually learn a string encoded in a function. Here's the"
" problem:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada tahun 1997, Ethan Bernstein dan Umesh Vazirani menggunakan algoritma "
"Deutsch-Jozsa untuk menyelesaikan masalah yang lebih spesifik dan terhad "
"berbanding masalah Deutsch-Jozsa. Daripada sekadar cuba membezakan antara "
"dua kelas fungsi yang berbeza, seperti dalam kes D-J, Bernstein dan Vazirani"
" menggunakan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa untuk benar-benar mempelajari rentetan "
"yang dikodkan dalam fungsi. Berikut adalah masalahnya:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ still takes an $n$-bit "
"string and outputs a single bit. But now, instead of promising that the "
"function is balanced or constant, we're now promised that the function is "
"the dot product between the input string $x$ and some secret $n$-bit string "
"$s$, modulo 2. (This dot product modulo 2 is called the \"binary dot "
"product.\") The problem is to figure out what the secret, $n$-bit string "
"is.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}^n \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ masih mengambil rentetan "
"$n$-bit dan mengeluarkan satu bit. Tetapi sekarang, daripada menjanjikan "
"bahawa fungsi itu seimbang atau malar, kita kini dijanjikan bahawa fungsi "
"itu adalah hasil darab titik antara rentetan input $x$ dan beberapa rentetan"
" $n$-bit rahsia $s$, modulo 2. (Hasil darab titik modulo 2 ini dipanggil "
"\"hasil darab titik binari.\") Masalahnya adalah untuk mengetahui apakah "
"rentetan $n$-bit rahsia itu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Written another way, we're given a black-box function $f: {0,1}^n "
"\\rightarrow {0,1}$ that satisfies $f(x) = s \\cdot x$ for some string $s$, "
"and we want to learn the string $s$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ditulis dengan cara lain, kita diberi fungsi kotak hitam $f: {0,1}^n "
"\\rightarrow {0,1}$ yang memenuhi $f(x) = s \\cdot x$ untuk beberapa "
"rentetan $s$, dan kita ingin mempelajari rentetan $s$ tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's take a look at how the D-J algorithm solves this problem:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita lihat bagaimana algoritma D-J menyelesaikan masalah ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, a Hadamard gate is applied to the $n$ input qubits, and a NOT gate "
"plus a Hadamard is applied to the output qubit, making the state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, get Hadamard digunakan pada $n$ qubit input, dan get NOT ditambah "
"Hadamard digunakan pada qubit output, menjadikan keadaan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle_{n} \\otimes |+\\rangle_{n-1} \\otimes |+\\rangle_{n-2} \\otimes ... \\otimes |+\\rangle_0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle_{n} \\otimes |+\\rangle_{n-1} \\otimes |+\\rangle_{n-2} \\otimes ... \\otimes |+\\rangle_0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The state of qubits 1 through $n$ can be written more simply as a sum "
"over all $2^n$ the $n$-qubit basis states $|00...00\\rangle, "
"|00...01\\rangle, |000...11\\rangle, ..., |111...11\\rangle$. We call the "
"set of these basis states $\\Sigma^n$. (See [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-"
"query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm) for more details.)\n"
msgstr ""
"   Keadaan qubit 1 hingga $n$ boleh ditulis dengan lebih mudah sebagai "
"jumlah ke atas semua $2^n$ keadaan basis $n$-qubit $|00...00\\rangle, "
"|00...01\\rangle, |000...11\\rangle, ..., |111...11\\rangle$. Kita panggil "
"set keadaan basis ini $\\Sigma^n$. (Lihat [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-"
"query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm) untuk maklumat lanjut.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}{|x\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}{|x\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the $U_f$ gate is applied to the qubits. This gate will take the first"
" n qubits as input (which are now in an equal superposition of all possible "
"n-bit strings) and applies the function $f(x)=s \\cdot x$ to the output "
"qubit, so that this qubit is now in the state: $ |- \\oplus f(x)\\rangle$. "
"Thanks to the phase kickback mechanism, the state of this qubit remains "
"unchanged, but some of the terms in the input qubit state pick up a minus "
"sign:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, get $U_f$ digunakan pada qubit. get ini akan mengambil $n$ qubit"
" pertama sebagai input (yang kini berada dalam superposisi sama rata semua "
"rentetan $n$-bit yang mungkin) dan menggunakan fungsi $f(x)=s \\cdot x$ pada"
" qubit output, supaya qubit ini kini berada dalam keadaan: $ |- \\oplus "
"f(x)\\rangle$. Berkat mekanisme phase kickback, keadaan qubit ini kekal "
"tidak berubah, tetapi sebahagian sebutan dalam keadaan qubit input mengambil"
" tanda tolak:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{f(x)}|x\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{f(x)}|x\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, the next set of Hadamards are applied to qubits 0 through $n-1$. "
"Keeping track of the minus signs in this case can be tricky. It's helpful to"
" know that applying a layer of Hadamards to $n$ qubits in a standard basis "
"state $|x\\rangle$ can be written as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, set Hadamard seterusnya digunakan pada qubit 0 hingga $n-1$. "
"Menjejaki tanda tolak dalam kes ini boleh menjadi rumit. Adalah berguna "
"untuk mengetahui bahawa menggunakan lapisan Hadamard pada $n$ qubit dalam "
"keadaan basis standard $|x\\rangle$ boleh ditulis sebagai:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} |x\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{y \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{x \\cdot y}|y\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} |x\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum\\limits_{y \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{x \\cdot y}|y\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So the state becomes:\n"
msgstr "Jadi keadaan menjadi:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}\\sum\\limits_{y \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{(s \\cdot x) + (x \\cdot y)}|y\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum\\limits_{x \\in \\Sigma^n}\\sum\\limits_{y \\in \\Sigma^n}{(-1)^{(s \\cdot x) + (x \\cdot y)}|y\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next step is to measure the first $n$ bits. But what will we measure? It "
"turns out that the state above simplifies to:  $|\\Psi\\rangle = |-\\rangle "
"\\otimes |s\\rangle$, but that's far from obvious. If you'd like to follow "
"through the math, see John Watrous' [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-"
"query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem) "
"course. The point is, though, that the phase kickback mechanism leads to the"
" input qubits being in the state $|s\\rangle$. So, to find out what the "
"secret string $s$ was, you simply need to measure the qubits!\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah seterusnya adalah mengukur $n$ bit pertama. Tetapi apakah yang akan "
"kita ukur? Rupanya, keadaan di atas memudah kepada: $|\\Psi\\rangle = "
"|-\\rangle \\otimes |s\\rangle$, tetapi itu jauh dari jelas. Jika anda ingin"
" mengikuti matemat tersebut, lihat kursus [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-"
"query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem) "
"oleh John Watrous. Intinya ialah mekanisme phase kickback menyebabkan qubit "
"input berada dalam keadaan $|s\\rangle$. Jadi, untuk mengetahui apakah "
"rentetan rahsia $s$ tersebut, anda hanya perlu mengukur qubit!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "Semak pemahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that the state from Step 3 above is indeed the state $|s\\rangle$ for"
" the special case of $n=1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sahkan bahawa keadaan dari Langkah 3 di atas memang keadaan $|s\\rangle$ "
"untuk kes khas $n=1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you explicitly write out the two summations, you should get a state "
"with four terms (let's omit the output state $|-\\rangle$ for this):\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila anda menulis secara eksplisit dua penjumlahan itu, anda sepatutnya "
"mendapat keadaan dengan empat sebutan (mari kita abaikan keadaan output "
"$|-\\rangle$ untuk ini):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2}[|0\\rangle + (-1)^s |0\\rangle + |1\\rangle + (-1)^{(s+1)} |1\\rangle]\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\Psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2}[|0\\rangle + (-1)^s |0\\rangle + |1\\rangle + (-1)^{(s+1)} |1\\rangle]\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $s=0$, then the first two terms add constructively and the last two terms"
" cancel, leaving us with $|\\Psi\\rangle = |0\\rangle$. If $s=1$, then the "
"last two terms add constructively and the first two terms cancel, leaving us"
" with $|\\Psi\\rangle = |1\\rangle$. So, in either case, $|\\Psi\\rangle = "
"|s\\rangle$. Hopefully this simplest case gives you a sense for how the "
"general case with $n$ qubits works: all terms that are not $|s\\rangle$ "
"interfere away, leaving just the state $|s\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $s=0$, maka dua sebutan pertama bertambah secara membina dan dua "
"sebutan terakhir dibatalkan, meninggalkan kita dengan $|\\Psi\\rangle = "
"|0\\rangle$. Jika $s=1$, maka dua sebutan terakhir bertambah secara membina "
"dan dua sebutan pertama dibatalkan, meninggalkan kita dengan $|\\Psi\\rangle"
" = |1\\rangle$. Jadi, dalam kedua-dua kes, $|\\Psi\\rangle = |s\\rangle$. "
"Mudah-mudahan kes paling mudah ini memberi anda gambaran tentang cara kes "
"umum dengan $n$ qubit berfungsi: semua sebutan yang bukan $|s\\rangle$ "
"saling mengganggu dan hilang, meninggalkan hanya keadaan $|s\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How can the same algorithm solve both the Bernstein-Vazirani and Deutsch-"
"Jozsa problems? To make sense of this, think about Bernstein-Vazirani "
"functions, which are of the form $f(x) = s \\cdot x$. Are these functions "
"also Deutsch-Jozsa functions? That is, determine whether functions of this "
"form satisfy the Deutsch-Jozsa problem promise: that they're either "
"*constant* or *balanced*. How does this help us understand how the same "
"algorithm solves two different problems?\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana algoritma yang sama boleh menyelesaikan kedua-dua masalah "
"Bernstein-Vazirani dan Deutsch-Jozsa? Untuk memahami ini, fikirkan tentang "
"fungsi Bernstein-Vazirani, yang berbentuk $f(x) = s \\cdot x$. Adakah "
"fungsi-fungsi ini juga merupakan fungsi Deutsch-Jozsa? Iaitu, tentukan sama "
"ada fungsi berbentuk ini memenuhi janji masalah Deutsch-Jozsa: bahawa ia "
"sama ada *malar* atau *seimbang*. Bagaimana ini membantu kita memahami cara "
"algoritma yang sama menyelesaikan dua masalah yang berbeza?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every Bernstein-Vazirani function of the form $f(x) = s \\cdot x$ also "
"satisfies the Deutsch-Jozsa problem promise: if s=00...00, then the function"
" is constant (always returns 0 for every string x). If s is any other "
"string, then the function is balanced. So, applying the Deutsch-Jozsa "
"algorithm to one of these functions simultaneously solves both problems! It "
"returns the string, and if that string is 00...00 then we know it's "
"constant; if there's at least one \"1\" in the string, we know it's "
"balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap fungsi Bernstein-Vazirani berbentuk $f(x) = s \\cdot x$ juga memenuhi"
" janji masalah Deutsch-Jozsa: jika s=00...00, maka fungsi itu malar "
"(sentiasa mengembalikan 0 untuk setiap rentetan x). Jika s adalah rentetan "
"lain, maka fungsi itu seimbang. Jadi, menggunakan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa "
"pada salah satu fungsi ini secara serentak menyelesaikan kedua-dua masalah! "
"Ia mengembalikan rentetan, dan jika rentetan itu adalah 00...00 maka kita "
"tahu ia malar; jika ada sekurang-kurangnya satu \"1\" dalam rentetan, kita "
"tahu ia seimbang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also verify that this algorithm successfully solves the Bernstein-"
"Vazirani problem by testing it experimentally. First, we create the B-V "
"function that lives inside the black box:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga boleh mengesahkan bahawa algoritma ini berjaya menyelesaikan "
"masalah Bernstein-Vazirani dengan mengujinya secara eksperimen. Pertama, "
"kita cipta fungsi B-V yang tinggal di dalam kotak hitam:\n"

